  "bank": "Reuse exact ranked_v1 104 physical policies, source-only proposal ranking, coordinates and provenance. Original73 prefix, round1 release89 and round2 release104. No regenerated proposals, reranking or task-dependent feasibility filtering.",
  "representation": "Same ranked104 physical policies, mean4/risk10 coordinates, eight source identities and source_risk_calibration_v1. All structural arms first replay both shared full-source initialization updates. Frozen-query and dual use identically initialized independent per-policy terminal mixtures. No source fitting, encoder reconstruction, coordinate change or proposal reranking.",
  "response_units": "Identity mapping for f,g-tau,log sigma_f^2,log sigma_g^2. Formula uses normalized control-group means and global SD, not a dimension sum. L,sigma,alpha,weights,tau are identical; changes caused by actual policy/group geometry are not response-unit rescaling.",
  "selection": "Preserve the original six arms. New frozen-query online uses the unchanged complete post-initialization query model for both order3 moment KG decisions: round1 available89/remaining360; round2 available104/remaining359. Its query mean, covariance, noise and identity weights never read search raw. Only its point-only terminal consumes each own raw observation; the query posterior paid count2 does not determine the actual remaining-call budget. No acquisition precision or terminal proxy change.",
  "terminal": "Unchanged point-only terminal for frozen-query, complete-model terminal for original full arm and original definitions for the other five arms. Each task has two STOP arms with360 verifier episodes and five online arms with358 each. Every arm has total362 logical calls. Freeze all112 recommendations before any verifier; finish all112 independent verifiers before explicit truth scoring.",
  "mechanism_diagnostic": "Primary dual minus frozen-query comparison tests whether reading search observations into the complete query posterior improves the two-query policy when both use the same point-only terminal mechanism. It includes queried-point learning and cross-policy propagation, not a pure cross-policy-only effect. Retain full, no-cross, STOP and GP references, independent executions, saved paths and query/terminal channel diagnostics.",
  "endpoints": "Main statistics use only the16 newly registered geometries. Report actual certified safe reward, conditional reward, false certificates and paired dual-minus-frozen-query difference; keep the other six-arm references. Record two-query paths, queried/unsampled and original/generated recommendation status, and query-versus-terminal prediction channels. No outcome-based stopping, replacement or extension; read truths only after all112 verifiers.",
  "randomness": "Draw exactly16 tasks once via original task_configs(seed2026101611). Public kwargs must differ from source00..07, nominal and the32 prior targets at seeds1561/1571/1581/1591/1601; report collisions without redraw. Seeds2026101612/13/14/15 independently control initialization/search/verification/bootstrap. Share two fresh initialization raws across seven arms per task; each of five online arms separately simulates and pays for two own search raws. Paired task/round/query random streams give equal raw for equal queries without borrowing calls. Verification is independent of search.",
  "accounting": "32 shared initialization +160 separately executed search +40160 independent verification =40352 new physical calls;112*362=40544 logical calls. Verification is16*(2*360+5*358). Each frozen-query raw updates only its terminal, but still costs one physical and one logical episode; its unchanged query posterior counter2 is not the arm resource counter. All new source/calibration/original-law/GP fits remain0. Preserve prior ledgers and record numerical work/failures separately.",
